      "writtenOn": "2026-10-01T15:58:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In zmake, host/llvm is an x86_64 host toolchain used for native_sim unit tests (zephyr/test/), whereas the 170+ physical boards (rex, geralt, etc.) are cross-compiled target builds (ARM/RISC-V) that configure against coreboot-sdk (arm-eabi-gcc, riscv64-elf-gcc).\n\nWhen building for coverage (opts.code_coverage), zmake builds the board libraries with coreboot-sdk to generate baseline zero-count tracefiles (all_builds.info), while Twister runs unit tests natively on host/llvm to generate execution hit counts (all_tests.info). Because lcov -a merges tracefiles at the text level by matching source file paths (SF:...) and line numbers (DA:...), the two combine cleanly regardless of target vs host compiler. (Verified in our CQ dry run which passed with Code-Coverage +1 and reduced runtime from 138m to 88m).\n\nI updated the commit message to document this distinction.",
      "parentUuid": "b64d0768_06c47252",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 50
      },
